            <valueName>layer:SOREM:1.0:Broadcast_Text</valueName>
            <value>At 7:25 p.m. Central Standard Time Friday, Environment Canada has updated a tornado warning for South Central Saskatchewan. Extra care and attention should be exercised. The following localities are included in the warning: Lanigan, Jansen, Semans, Duval, Govan, Nokomis, Wynyard, Elfros, Foam Lake, Ituna, Lestock, Wishart, Punnichy and Raymore. Environment Canada meteorologists are tracking a severe thunderstorm that is producing a tornado. Damaging winds, large hail and locally intense rainfall are also possible. Take cover immediately if threatening weather approaches. Please consult local media for more information.</value>
        </parameter>
